WHERE THIS COMES FROM
---------------------

Gaffer is built on the work of other open-source projects, all MIT licensed.
Each one's licence is kept in THIRD-PARTY/, and travels inside Gaffer.app.

* lumen-studio, by Ritik (Rkcr7). Gaffer's light service and web interface
  start from a copy of it: the Godox driver, model and gel tables, effects,
  scenes, schedules, cues and the web studio.
  https://github.com/Rkcr7/lumen-studio
  Copied from commit 8175526 into service/gaffer/ (renamed from
  src/lumen_studio), web/ and service/tests/. The first commit of the copy
  holds it unmodified; later commits show every change made here.
  Its own NOTICE, which asks for the credits below, is in
  THIRD-PARTY/lumen-studio/NOTICE.

* godox-ul60bi-bt, by Matt Harrison. The Python library and CLI that first
  spoke the Godox Bluetooth Mesh protocol: provisioning, keys, encryption and
  the vendor command set.
  https://github.com/mattharrison/godox-ul60bi-bt

* ha-godox-mesh, by Simon Cheng. The Home Assistant fork that extended that
  library from one light to the whole Godox mesh range and generated the
  per-model capability and gel tables. service/packages/godox-mesh-bt/ is
  that library at v0.2.8, as lumen-studio carries it, unchanged.
  https://github.com/binary-person/ha-godox-mesh

* ha-godox-ble-mesh, by SegulaLabs. Its meshimport.py, which reads the Godox
  app's mesh export, is the base of service/gaffer/godox_import.py.
  https://github.com/SegulaLabs/ha-godox-ble-mesh (commit 5c90e25)

* HA-Zhiyun-Light, by didim99. Zhiyun light name prefixes used by the scan.
  https://github.com/didim99/HA-Zhiyun-Light

* zhiyun-light-control, by aaditagrawal. Zhiyun protocol.
  https://github.com/aaditagrawal/zhiyun-light-control

* yongnuo-light-control, by asidjwiaijd. The Yongnuo name rule used by the scan.
  https://github.com/asidjwiaijd/yongnuo-light-control

